WEBVTT

00:02.290 --> 00:03.380
What the...

00:03.380 --> 00:05.140
Who the hell is that?

00:09.740 --> 00:10.810
Wait.

00:11.130 --> 00:15.820
If he were here to kill, 
someone would already be dead.

00:15.820 --> 00:17.860
So, we'll be okay?

00:18.380 --> 00:19.450
I guess we'll see.

00:21.490 --> 00:24.960
Trying to guess what Lemmings 
is thinking is a waste of time.

00:25.420 --> 00:26.310
Iwa-san.

00:30.380 --> 00:33.760
Either way, he's on the 
nationwide wanted list.

00:34.000 --> 00:36.550
Let's beat him down and put him in custody.

00:36.780 --> 00:40.260
Don't forget, we technically have witnesses.

00:40.260 --> 00:42.010
Polka-kun, Polka-kun.

00:42.010 --> 00:46.440
I think that guy's probably 
a lot scarier than the cops.

00:46.440 --> 00:47.530
Yes.

00:47.530 --> 00:48.900
I can tell.

00:51.730 --> 00:53.850
<i>Are those the ghosts of people he's killed?</i>

00:54.290 --> 00:57.070
<i>They're torn between... hatred and fear?</i>

01:04.020 --> 01:04.560
Wha—?!

01:10.250 --> 01:11.650
You've got strong arms.

01:12.800 --> 01:14.810
Have you been working out your core, too?

01:21.720 --> 01:25.010
I <i>did</i> remind you we've got witnesses, yeah?

01:35.550 --> 01:37.310
Take me seriously, damn it.

01:38.510 --> 01:39.340
Huh?

01:45.470 --> 01:47.140
Who, me?

01:49.670 --> 01:52.630
Huh? Is this some new kind of pickup routine?

01:52.630 --> 01:53.440
Misaki-chan!

01:53.780 --> 01:54.380
<i>I mustn't.</i>

01:54.890 --> 01:59.340
<i>If those officials see my magic, 
peace will slip through my fingers.</i>

01:59.700 --> 02:01.800
<i>Perhaps permanently.</i>

02:08.600 --> 02:09.850
<i>And regardless,</i>

02:09.850 --> 02:12.520
<i>I'll never have peace if 
I oppose that monster.</i>

02:16.820 --> 02:17.610
Arase!

02:17.830 --> 02:21.570
<i>He's similar to Shagrua,
although differently inclined.</i>

02:22.010 --> 02:25.480
<i>Though human, he's pushed beyond human limits.</i>

02:26.030 --> 02:28.790
<i>Thus, I'm left with only one choice:</i>

02:29.180 --> 02:31.520
<i>Forsake the girl and flee.</i>

02:38.860 --> 02:39.970
Polka-kun!

02:40.360 --> 02:42.560
<i>Maybe I messed up my reincarnation.</i>

02:43.430 --> 02:49.340
Teacher, it seems I've become quite a fool.

04:23.200 --> 04:24.820
What the hell is <i>that</i>?!

04:26.700 --> 04:27.470
Huh?!

04:32.070 --> 04:33.190
Polka-kun?

04:33.190 --> 04:35.580
I can't see, but that <i>is</i> you, isn't it?

04:35.580 --> 04:38.320
Quiet! Let's get out while we can.

04:41.340 --> 04:43.630
What? What was that noise?!

04:51.120 --> 04:53.310
He can see in pitch darkness?!

05:22.840 --> 05:23.780
Misaki-chan!

05:25.700 --> 05:26.490
Huh?

05:28.430 --> 05:31.430
Well, umm, see...

05:31.430 --> 05:33.540
I can't tell you that!

05:33.540 --> 05:35.640
I'd get chewed out if I did!

05:35.890 --> 05:39.360
So, end of discussion! Better luck next time!

05:42.690 --> 05:44.430
Hey, hold up!

05:44.430 --> 05:46.720
He's got nothing to do with this—
or any bad stuff.

05:49.850 --> 05:51.860
Well? I told you.

05:51.860 --> 05:53.120
Satisfied now?

05:53.120 --> 05:55.370
I'll even throw in a freebie!

05:56.860 --> 05:58.370
<i>Her paralytic saliva?!</i>

06:02.040 --> 06:05.340
I can't bite through these bandages.

06:05.340 --> 06:06.800
Psych!

06:15.040 --> 06:18.190
Lucky you. That was basically a kiss.

06:20.640 --> 06:24.920
Of course, a fork won't carry enough 
saliva to fully immobilize him.

06:27.400 --> 06:29.600
But thank you.

06:45.420 --> 06:48.320
You bought me time to 
work out a spell in peace.

07:01.640 --> 07:03.110
What the hell?

07:03.110 --> 07:06.140
We might as well not have been here,
 for all the good we did.

07:06.140 --> 07:08.570
Let's come in full gear next time.

07:08.570 --> 07:11.030
Oh, my. That's awfully extreme.

07:14.690 --> 07:20.830
Sorry, but after what I just saw, 
I haven't got the balls to come back unarmed.

07:23.930 --> 07:25.700
This is a non-smoking area.

07:25.700 --> 07:26.350
Huh?

07:30.930 --> 07:32.380
So, you're back,

07:32.640 --> 07:33.790
Lemmings.

07:34.690 --> 07:38.950
You were gone a long time. 
I expect quicker work from you.

07:42.140 --> 07:43.350
What?

07:43.630 --> 07:47.070
I see. So Jinba was already killed.

07:47.740 --> 07:51.240
Well, it never mattered 
to me who disposed of him.

07:52.080 --> 07:55.410
I continue to have high hopes for you, Nezu.

07:58.090 --> 07:59.550
Is there something else?

08:04.650 --> 08:05.830
For real?!

08:06.050 --> 08:09.160
That guy's like an urban 
legend here in Shinjuku.

08:09.710 --> 08:13.530
He slips in unnoticed and 
does his job without a fuss.

08:13.530 --> 08:16.640
Because he can pop up anywhere, 
they name him after a horde of rodents—

08:16.640 --> 08:18.890
"Lemmings."

08:19.280 --> 08:21.780
Man, I can't believe you 
made it out in one piece.

08:21.780 --> 08:24.720
Yeah, we made a real killing!

08:24.720 --> 08:29.210
<i>Still, you must've used a lot 
of magic power on that, Polka.</i>

08:29.570 --> 08:30.610
Yes.

08:31.100 --> 08:36.910
But the ghosts haunting that bandaged 
man more than made up for it.

08:46.250 --> 08:47.380
Thank you.

08:47.380 --> 08:49.210
Huh? What for?

08:49.460 --> 08:51.420
You protected me.

08:52.040 --> 08:55.340
You told him a secret, didn't you?

08:55.340 --> 08:57.560
Don't sweat it.

08:57.560 --> 08:59.430
You bailed me out, too,

08:59.750 --> 09:00.980
so we're even!

09:03.320 --> 09:06.030
It doesn't matter if you've known 
someone one second or five years.

09:06.490 --> 09:09.060
If you want to help them, go ahead and do it.

09:10.650 --> 09:14.690
Boy, I suspect you'll live a long time.

09:15.300 --> 09:18.820
So long that the distinction between 
a second and a century blurs.

09:19.460 --> 09:23.440
So don't bother worrying 
about how long a thing lasts.

09:23.850 --> 09:28.110
As you live on and on,
the force of habit and experience

09:28.110 --> 09:32.090
will take control when it matters most.

09:34.900 --> 09:38.200
With this frail body, I can't protect anyone.

09:38.650 --> 09:40.210
Not even myself.

09:41.370 --> 09:42.390
Misaki-chan.

09:43.310 --> 09:44.460
<i>Takumi-kun.</i>

09:45.140 --> 09:45.770
<i>And...</i>

09:46.110 --> 09:47.770
the real Polka-kun.

09:48.580 --> 09:54.030
I don't know the first thing about this world,
 so I want you to teach me.

09:54.540 --> 09:56.150
<i>About yourselves, as well.</i>

09:56.150 --> 09:58.360
What're you acting all formal for?

09:58.630 --> 10:00.570
I see clearly now.

10:01.070 --> 10:03.040
I don't want any peace

10:03.480 --> 10:08.790
that requires sacrificing someone who 
laughed with me, no matter how briefly.

10:18.890 --> 10:21.440
I can't believe you're still alive.

10:21.440 --> 10:23.510
You had me completely fooled,

10:23.750 --> 10:24.620
Polka.

10:25.980 --> 10:28.510
Playtime is over.

10:31.430 --> 10:32.940
And so,

10:32.940 --> 10:35.070
I've decided to start a business.

10:35.070 --> 10:36.230
What for?

10:36.560 --> 10:38.590
What happened yesterday 
drove it home for me.

10:38.910 --> 10:45.440
To live here peacefully, with limited mana,
I really do need money.

10:45.440 --> 10:47.410
Talk about materialistic.

10:47.410 --> 10:50.650
Are you gonna make more big skeletons?!

10:50.650 --> 10:52.630
They'll call in the riot squad.

10:52.630 --> 10:57.930
Necromancy is useful in combat,
but that isn't all it's good for.

10:58.240 --> 11:01.630
For instance, if I make pacts with 
ghosts who still have a sense of self,

11:01.630 --> 11:04.430
I can let them possess and move objects.

11:04.430 --> 11:06.750
Hey, that's my mechanical pencil.

11:06.750 --> 11:08.770
You dropped it, so I borrowed it.

11:08.770 --> 11:09.770
No problem!

11:09.980 --> 11:15.990
I found a sane ghost in the basement, 
so I made a pact and let it possess this.

11:16.480 --> 11:17.880
Whoa!

11:19.440 --> 11:22.320
I say. I'm honored to meet acquaintances
 of Clarissa, the famed intermediary.

11:22.670 --> 11:24.370
It's way more eloquent than I expected!

11:25.720 --> 11:31.500
<b>My name is Hosorogi,
and I passed away here five years ago.
Heh heh heh..
I bet you could dupe a land swindler
 and legally flip this building...</b>

11:28.150 --> 11:29.160
Wow!

11:29.160 --> 11:31.130
But it's saying some shady-ass things!

11:31.500 --> 11:35.820
Since only I can use magic, 
if I start a business with magic,

11:35.820 --> 11:38.170
I may be able to corner the market.

11:38.170 --> 11:41.040
In fact, I've already drawn up a sign.

11:41.550 --> 11:43.430
<b>THE
SHOP</b>

11:41.550 --> 11:43.430
<b>We
 do 
things</b>

11:41.550 --> 11:43.430
<b>Magic? No problem</b>

11:41.550 --> 11:43.430
<b>Yay!!</b>

11:43.430 --> 11:44.530
What do you think?

11:43.430 --> 11:46.640
<b>THE SHOP</b>

11:43.430 --> 11:46.640
<b>We 
do
things</b>

11:43.430 --> 11:46.640
<b>Magic?
 No problem!</b>

11:43.430 --> 11:46.640
<b>Yay!!</b>

11:44.530 --> 11:46.640
I helped!

11:46.640 --> 11:49.100
You wanna live peacefully, yeah?

11:51.620 --> 11:57.350
I know you're really a freaky 
monster who could kill me no sweat,

11:57.350 --> 11:58.500
but I'll say this anyway.

11:59.930 --> 12:01.530
Are you out of your mind?

12:01.530 --> 12:02.850
What?

12:04.870 --> 12:07.330
If it's money you're after, I have a better idea.

12:11.460 --> 12:13.420
Fortunes

12:11.980 --> 12:13.050
I can see it now.

12:14.300 --> 12:16.420
Your profession

12:16.420 --> 12:18.730
is related to medicine, is it not?

12:19.170 --> 12:20.420
Yeah, it is.

12:20.420 --> 12:23.510
I sense that the flow of qi 
is blocked in your left leg.

12:23.510 --> 12:28.010
Y-You're right! I broke it,
and I'm still in physical therapy.

12:28.010 --> 12:29.620
It moves on its own?!

12:30.810 --> 12:33.270
Don't play so many video games.

12:31.130 --> 12:33.270
"Don't play so many video games"?

12:33.270 --> 12:36.170
Is there anything you <i>don't</i> know?!

12:38.410 --> 12:40.780
I can't believe you're actually raking it in.

12:40.780 --> 12:42.390
Amazing, right?!

12:42.390 --> 12:46.240
You'd never guess that sign 
was all done in pencil.

12:46.240 --> 12:48.790
You made a hundred grand in a week.

12:49.270 --> 12:51.210
But really, fortune telling?

12:52.120 --> 12:58.040
The keys to sham fortune telling are 
hot reading and cold reading.
Hot reading = Passing off the results
of prior investigation as guesses.
Cold reading = Guessing a subject's thoughts
 based on what they say and do. 

 You will need: 
 - A crystal ball 
 - Exotic costumes

12:52.120 --> 12:58.040
"The keys to sham fortune telling 
are hot reading and cold reading"?

12:58.270 --> 13:00.000
Honestly, this is a great setup.

13:00.840 --> 13:05.150
I look up clients, using the names and 
birth dates we make them write at the desk,

13:05.590 --> 13:08.280
and show Polka the data through 
this little eyeball guy.

13:08.850 --> 13:11.270
And with Polka doing his thing on top of that...

13:11.720 --> 13:14.940
I died last month of overeating.

13:14.940 --> 13:18.720
I see you lost someone 
dear to you last month.

13:18.720 --> 13:20.150
How did you know?!

13:22.340 --> 13:28.570
The key to open a new door is carved on 
a tombstone at the back of your garden.

13:28.570 --> 13:29.930
A tombstone?

13:30.940 --> 13:33.580
You mean the one for our pet, 
Mii-chan, who died last year?

13:33.810 --> 13:38.300
Could it be... the combination 
to the main safe?

13:41.730 --> 13:45.130
...you get fortune telling with 
a 100% accuracy rate.

13:45.420 --> 13:50.250
Still, you writing on your own 
has to look like a total gimmick.

13:51.760 --> 13:56.230
<b>That's just what we want. 
Let them start out suspicious 
and then decide it's real magic.
 That will lay the groundwork for 
more potent brainwashing to come.
 Heh heh heh...</b>

13:56.230 --> 13:58.000
Brainwashing?

14:00.350 --> 14:03.180
You <i>do</i> remember Polka wants peace, right?

14:05.440 --> 14:07.990
This is the first money I've earned here.

14:10.450 --> 14:12.490
Now to split it five ways.

14:12.490 --> 14:13.580
Why five?

14:13.580 --> 14:18.460
For me, Misaki-chan, Takumi-kun, 
the real Polka-kun, and Hosorogi-san.

14:18.460 --> 14:20.420
You sure are conscientious.

14:20.420 --> 14:21.880
Yay!

14:23.300 --> 14:24.860
What's wrong?

14:24.860 --> 14:28.330
Just think of it as a token of 
thanks for lending me your body.

14:29.260 --> 14:31.960
Is he saying he doesn't want the money?

14:31.960 --> 14:34.830
Yes. He says he didn't earn it.

14:34.830 --> 14:38.230
Well, the real Polka's probably 
seen enough cash for a lifetime.

14:39.740 --> 14:43.770
Oh, right. You can't access all his memories.

14:44.160 --> 14:46.100
Polka Shinoyama's family is—

14:47.750 --> 14:49.570
Hey, what's the big idea?

14:49.570 --> 14:53.030
Oh, dear, are we disturbing you?

14:53.260 --> 14:55.750
Good day, everyone.

14:56.580 --> 14:59.670
There he is! Polka really is here!

15:02.310 --> 15:05.630
It's been half a month, 
hasn't it, Uncle Polka?

15:05.630 --> 15:07.370
<i>What? Could it be...?!</i>

15:11.110 --> 15:11.740
Kazuki
Shinoyama

15:11.190 --> 15:15.980
<i>Kazuki and Shizuki Shinoyama, twin siblings.</i>

15:12.740 --> 15:18.770
Shizuki
Shinoyama

15:15.080 --> 15:18.770
Kazuki
Shinoyama

15:16.320 --> 15:18.330
<i>They're this body's niece and nephew!</i>

15:18.770 --> 15:20.940
<i>Oh, no! I've got to fool them!</i>

15:23.130 --> 15:27.820
You must be mistaken. I am the Corpse God,

15:28.160 --> 15:32.030
a sorcerer strayed into your 
world from far beyond the veil.

15:32.030 --> 15:34.080
Excuse me? Who do you think you're fooling?

15:34.080 --> 15:36.740
And what's with that name?

15:36.740 --> 15:39.930
"Corpse God"? A god for dead bodies?

15:40.810 --> 15:42.340
That's... kinda cool.

15:42.340 --> 15:43.710
You think so?

15:43.710 --> 15:46.330
Calm down, Shizuki.

15:46.780 --> 15:50.330
These peasants must have put him up to it.

15:50.660 --> 15:56.140
Why else would Uncle Polka 
have run away from home?

15:56.380 --> 15:57.770
<i>This is bad.</i>

15:57.770 --> 16:01.350
<i>If they find out I'm not him inside,
 there goes my peace.</i>

16:01.690 --> 16:04.810
Well, let's set that aside for now.

16:05.040 --> 16:07.770
We're here as customers today.

16:09.730 --> 16:12.170
Won't you show us

16:13.450 --> 16:15.650
your oh-so-impressive fortune telling?

16:17.290 --> 16:18.890
A foolish question.

16:18.890 --> 16:23.040
All things have their proper time.

16:23.420 --> 16:25.260
Call again later.

16:25.260 --> 16:28.030
We open at 10 a.m. tomorrow.

16:28.670 --> 16:32.220
So, why don't you leave 
for today, little girl?

16:32.430 --> 16:34.700
Oh? How odd.

16:34.700 --> 16:38.350
I don't recall giving 
you permission to speak.

16:38.600 --> 16:41.690
A mere peasant presumes to argue with <i>me</i>?

16:42.020 --> 16:45.600
And what do you propose to do if I refuse?

16:45.600 --> 16:48.800
Well, call the cops, for a start.

16:48.800 --> 16:49.610
Huh?

16:49.610 --> 16:54.640
What did you expect? You barged 
into a business after closing time.

16:55.090 --> 16:59.150
What's a poor, frightened peasant 
like me to do but call the cops?

17:00.330 --> 17:02.340
What nonsense.

17:02.340 --> 17:04.710
Do you have any idea who we are?

17:04.710 --> 17:09.500
Classless nouveaux riches who look down 
their noses at people they've just met?

17:09.500 --> 17:10.630
I am—

17:10.630 --> 17:12.710
Please be calm, little miss!

17:12.710 --> 17:17.800
He's probably recording this conversation!
Maybe even streaming it.

17:17.800 --> 17:20.410
Giving your name might be unwise.

17:21.360 --> 17:22.460
What now?

17:22.460 --> 17:27.730
Are you gonna sic your men in black 
on me because you lost an argument?

17:28.430 --> 17:29.660
I've had it with your—

17:29.660 --> 17:31.980
That's enough. Thank you.

17:32.380 --> 17:36.450
I realize you're making 
yourself a target to spare me,

17:36.680 --> 17:39.560
but this child is on the verge of tears.

17:40.820 --> 17:42.240
Th-That's ridiculous!

17:47.090 --> 17:48.120
Hey, Polka! What're you—

17:51.370 --> 17:53.760
You said you wanted your fortunes read.

17:54.240 --> 17:57.360
Don't worry. You both have a future.

17:58.010 --> 18:00.220
I'll protect you.

18:00.220 --> 18:04.140
Th-That's rich coming from you, Polka!

18:04.140 --> 18:05.570
You're mistaken.

18:06.180 --> 18:09.150
But I am acquainted with Polka.

18:09.520 --> 18:11.110
And he told me that

18:12.070 --> 18:14.070
he'll return home tomorrow.

18:16.490 --> 18:20.210
So you should go home for today, as well.

18:20.210 --> 18:22.910
Help... Help...

18:22.910 --> 18:27.120
<i>Yes, I understand. You have 
nothing to worry about.</i>

18:27.120 --> 18:33.500
Someone, help these children.

18:33.730 --> 18:34.510
Yes.

18:35.180 --> 18:37.660
I'll keep these children safe.

18:40.850 --> 18:44.430
"Evil spirit" isn't quite 
the right word for her.

18:44.850 --> 18:49.800
She seems to want to protect the twins,
but she's gone half-mad.

18:49.800 --> 18:52.260
And you trust a ghost like that?

18:52.260 --> 18:54.060
I can't ignore this.

18:54.060 --> 18:56.610
You seem awfully soft on those kids.

18:56.610 --> 18:59.030
Yes, well...

19:00.420 --> 19:03.740
They remind me of some other 
children who tried to act tough.

19:03.740 --> 19:05.740
Oh, I see.

19:05.740 --> 19:06.950
Hey, so,

19:07.240 --> 19:10.520
are you really going back to 
Polka-kun's house tomorrow?

19:10.520 --> 19:11.340
Yes.

19:11.340 --> 19:13.290
Where does he live?

19:13.760 --> 19:15.210
Um, let me think.

19:15.210 --> 19:16.070
Here.

19:16.070 --> 19:16.960
Huh?

19:17.610 --> 19:19.260
The Shinoyama Group.

19:19.580 --> 19:23.770
Built around Shinoyama Bank, 
it has assets in the trillions.

19:19.700 --> 19:24.030
<b>Shinoyama Bank</b>

19:24.280 --> 19:28.070
They're not the richest people out there, 
but they're still loaded.

19:28.070 --> 19:30.300
And you, Polka,

19:30.640 --> 19:35.580
are the second son of their current 
patriarch, Rozan Shinoyama.

19:37.320 --> 19:40.740
Your father, Rozan, turned 79 this year.

19:40.990 --> 19:43.380
And if something happened to him,

19:43.380 --> 19:46.280
Polka could claim a share of his inheritance.

19:47.030 --> 19:49.750
No wonder someone wants you dead.

19:51.090 --> 19:53.120
But my peaceful life...

19:53.720 --> 19:56.290
Why's the real one look shocked, too?

19:56.570 --> 20:00.840
Like I said before, we don't 
know who put the hit on Polka.

20:01.230 --> 20:04.840
But it could have been one of your relatives.

20:05.330 --> 20:09.120
Going home is like charging 
into enemy territory.

20:09.120 --> 20:10.430
Are you sure about this?

20:11.030 --> 20:14.150
Oh, come on. Polka-kun can handle it.

20:14.150 --> 20:16.810
Only if he can afford to 
use magic out in the open.

20:16.810 --> 20:19.980
Oh, I had bodyguards back when I was alive.

20:20.280 --> 20:24.080
A zombie saber-toothed tiger 
and a skeleton heavy cavalry soldier.

20:24.080 --> 20:26.910
This is sounding less peaceful by the word.

20:28.450 --> 20:29.580
I'm a silent bodyguard. Please don't pry.

20:29.580 --> 20:35.080
I'm a silent 
bodyguard.
Please don't pry.

20:30.100 --> 20:31.240
How about this?

20:31.240 --> 20:35.080
Any rich guy who'd buy that 
would go broke in no time.

20:35.080 --> 20:36.370
Hmm...

20:36.370 --> 20:39.420
Then I'll need a bodyguard who looks human.

20:39.760 --> 20:41.840
Who looks human...

20:40.660 --> 20:41.840
Ooh!

20:43.840 --> 20:45.750
Huh? What's up?

20:46.670 --> 20:48.600
What's wrong with Polka?!

20:48.870 --> 20:52.490
Who does that wimp think he is,
acting all grown up?!

20:53.360 --> 20:57.020
Was that really Uncle Polka, do you think?

21:03.640 --> 21:05.350
Takeru-oniisama.

21:05.810 --> 21:09.830
You shouldn't be out playing 
so late, Kazuki, Shizuki.

21:10.460 --> 21:11.690
We're terribly sorry.

21:11.690 --> 21:13.830
S-Sorry.

21:13.830 --> 21:17.180
Now, tell me. Did Polka seem well?

21:17.180 --> 21:19.020
Huh? Y-Yeah.

21:19.020 --> 21:21.300
He said to expect him at home tomorrow.

21:21.300 --> 21:24.710
I see. That's something to look forward to.

21:25.260 --> 21:29.200
Although, that said,
I'll have to assign him a babysitter.

21:29.890 --> 21:31.850
The two of you should take care, as well.

21:32.950 --> 21:37.950
There could always be another accident,
like what happened to Suzuka.

23:15.180 --> 23:18.700
I see. So, Polka's alive and kicking.

23:19.260 --> 23:23.210
Still, playing magician in Shinjuku?

23:23.690 --> 23:26.130
He must have gotten that from you,

23:26.630 --> 23:27.590
Kanon.

23:30.240 --> 23:34.220
I suppose I can't die just yet.
